To add the digits of a number in MATLAB, you can convert the number to a string, then iterate over each character, convert it back to a digit, and sum them up. Here's a simple way to do it:

```matlab
function sum = digitSum(n)
    strNum = num2str(n);
    sum = 0;
    for i = 1:length(strNum)
        if strNum(i) ~= '.'
            sum = sum + str2double(strNum(i));
        end
    end
end
```

This function will sum the digits of the number `n`.

